#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0535 expect=noViolation domain=DS
#note "EMPTY-DATASET PIN, re-noted under PLAN-zero-row-routing-rekey.md (owner rulings Q1 / Q5 / 6c-1, Fix #349 / EC-89; policy text: lib/corej-cdisc-rules/documentation/zero-row-policy.md). DS declared WITHOUT DSSCAT (the sharpest case: the rule's negative-polarity leaf not var_exists(\"DSSCAT\") is TRUE on the real metadata) and with ZERO data rows. Ruled: the other two conjuncts -- not is_unique_set(DSCAT, keys=[USUBJID, EPOCH]) and DSCAT == \"DISPOSITION EVENT\" -- must read rows, so the rule has nothing to check and returns EXECUTED with zero findings, never SKIPPED. The metadata leaf alone cannot fire the AND; the row path over the real 0-row table yields no bits. The empty DS is reported once, by CDISC-CG0408."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSCAT    type=Char label="Category for Disposition Event"
col EPOCH    type=Char label="Epoch"
---
